From: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 13:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] uvcvideo: add bandwidth_cap module parameter

The Good Penguin's out-of-tree patch, rebased on 6.18: cap the
isochronous bandwidth a UVC device may reserve, in bytes per frame
(0 = unlimited, the default). Cheap cameras report an inflated
dwMaxPayloadTransferSize (often the maximum alt setting) regardless of
the negotiated format, so the driver parks every stream at the largest
alt setting and the host controller's periodic budget is exhausted by a
single camera. With a cap set, alt selection picks the smallest alt
setting that covers the cap instead — the user asserts the real
bandwidth of the configured mode.

Set at runtime:
  echo 2400 > /sys/module/uvcvideo/parameters/bandwidth_cap
(2400 B/frame = 153.6 Mbps), or at boot with
uvcvideo.bandwidth_cap=2400 on the kernel command line. Inert by
default (0 = unlimited).

Signed-off-by: monoflow-ayvu <dev@ayvu>
---
 drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
index dfa1b5fe48dc..7e55c234e4e5 100644
--- a/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/usb/uvc/uvc_video.c
@@ -24,6 +24,12 @@
 
 #include "uvcvideo.h"
 
+static unsigned int uvc_bandwidth_cap;
+module_param_named(bandwidth_cap, uvc_bandwidth_cap, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(bandwidth_cap,
+	"Cap on per-device isochronous bandwidth in bytes per frame "
+	"(0 = unlimited). Alt setting selection uses min(device-reported, cap).");
+
 /* ------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * UVC Controls
  */
@@ -2014,6 +2014,13 @@ static int uvc_video_start_transfer(struct uvc_streaming *stream,
 				bandwidth);
 		}
 
+		if (uvc_bandwidth_cap > 0 && bandwidth > uvc_bandwidth_cap) {
+			uvc_dbg(stream->dev, VIDEO,
+				"Capping bandwidth from %u to %u B/frame (bandwidth_cap)\n",
+				bandwidth, uvc_bandwidth_cap);
+			bandwidth = uvc_bandwidth_cap;
+		}
+
 		for (i = 0; i < intf->num_altsetting; ++i) {
 			struct usb_host_interface *alts;
 			unsigned int psize;
